ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "vLLM", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/design/prefix_caching.md", overlap: "Automatic prefix/KV cache reuse for repeated prompt prefixes; reduces serving cost but does not select receiver-role-relevant spans or compress inter-agent messages."},
  {system: "SGLang", url: "https://arxiv.org/html/2312.07104v1", overlap: "RadixAttention/prefix reuse for efficient LLM programs; systems-side reuse, not receiver-role-conditioned extractive filtering."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "KV-cache storage/reuse/offload for LLM serving; no semantic role-conditioned message span selection."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "KV-cache reuse optimization; no inter-agent content filtering."},
  {system: "Microsoft LLMLingua / LongLLMLingua", url: "https://github.com/microsoft/LLMLingua", overlap: "Shipping/open generic prompt compression baseline; role-agnostic or question/context-aware compression, but not specifically receiver-role-conditioned inter-agent span filtering."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: insufficient evidence for realistic workload. EXP-0023 is a CPU synthetic simulation with task-success defined as retained act-on token mass, not end-to-end receiver action/tool correctness. The reported effect reverses in high-verbosity cells: role-conditioned minus generic is -0.053 at verb_frac=0.8, and generic significantly beats role-conditioned in 12/36 cells. The load-bearing unknown, real act-on-to-salience correlation in AutoGen/CrewAI/LangGraph-style traces, is explicitly unmeasured.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. I found no evidence that vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM ship the claimed receiver-role-conditioned inter-agent span filter; their overlap is serving-side KV/prefix/cache efficiency, not semantic compression. However, the mechanism is mostly application glue over existing generic prompt compression plus multi-agent routing metadata, not a demonstrated systems design. The packet’s own evidence only supports a conditional mechanism: role-conditioning wins mainly when role/task predicts act-on spans well, AUC roughly >=0.65, and verbosity is low-to-moderate; it fails where the narrative predicted the largest gain. Reproducibility is acceptable for L0 artifacts, but the artifact does not establish scale behavior, real workload validity, or a systems contribution beyond integrating a role-conditioned scorer with an existing compression pipeline.
